WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.767 --> 00:00:01.901
-Welcome back.

00:00:01.901 --> 00:00:02.934
You look gorgeous.
Thanks for being here.

00:00:02.934 --> 00:00:04.267
-Thank you.
Back in the studio.

00:00:04.267 --> 00:00:06.067
-In person!
-I know.

00:00:06.067 --> 00:00:07.968
-I haven't seen you --
We Zoomed.

00:00:07.968 --> 00:00:10.801
-We Zoomed a couple times,
yes, during lockdown.

00:00:10.801 --> 00:00:12.200
-Yeah, thank you for doing that
for us.

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:13.968
I appreciate that.
-It felt like I was sort of

00:00:13.968 --> 00:00:15.734
a part of history.
Like, I don't know how many

00:00:15.734 --> 00:00:17.934
people have done
"The Tonight Show" over Zoom.

00:00:17.934 --> 00:00:19.167
-It was weird times.
-But I feel like I'm a part of

00:00:19.167 --> 00:00:20.534
an exclusive group.
-You are.

00:00:20.534 --> 00:00:22.367
Yeah, you're part of the fam.
-Yeah.

00:00:22.367 --> 00:00:24.000
-We love having -- thanks for
playing "Catch Phrase," too.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:26.467
That was intense.
-Oh, I love games like that.

00:00:26.467 --> 00:00:28.267
-You do?
-"Catch Phrase," "Heads Up."

00:00:28.267 --> 00:00:31.901
You know, I make people
on the set play those games

00:00:31.901 --> 00:00:33.868
all the time.
I think they get sick of it.

00:00:33.868 --> 00:00:37.000
-We celebrated, I hugged Conan,
I could feel his heart beating.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:38.133
[ Laughter ]

00:00:38.133 --> 00:00:39.801
Honestly, about to have
a heart attack.

00:00:39.801 --> 00:00:40.868
Intense.
-It is.

00:00:40.868 --> 00:00:42.834
It's very --
It's a lot of adrenaline.

00:00:42.834 --> 00:00:44.267
-Slip N' Slide --
that was unbelievable.

00:00:44.267 --> 00:00:45.767
-I still can't believe
you got "cyborg."

00:00:45.767 --> 00:00:47.901
-Here's the thing.
Like, when we play that game,

00:00:47.901 --> 00:00:51.400
you often forget that you're
able to be physical, as well.

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:53.000
-Yeah.
-It's true.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:55.400
-But how did you get "cyborg"?

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:57.200
-Dude, we were locked in.
-We were.

00:00:57.200 --> 00:00:58.234
We were at that point.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:58.234 --> 00:01:00.133
-"Cyborg"?
I would never get that.

00:01:00.133 --> 00:01:02.267
I would've lost the game,
"cyborg."

00:01:02.267 --> 00:01:05.200
Dude, "It's a bird game"?
[ Laughter ]

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:07.801
I can't even --
We'll talk some other time.

00:01:07.801 --> 00:01:09.067
But first, let's talk about you.

00:01:09.067 --> 00:01:10.601
Let's talk about "Westworld,"
please.

00:01:10.601 --> 00:01:12.033
It's finally back.
It's coming back Sunday.

00:01:12.033 --> 00:01:13.601
-It's back.
We're back, baby.

00:01:13.601 --> 00:01:15.400
Yeah, season four.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:17.100
-Wow.

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:20.467
Fans are waiting two years
for this new season.

00:01:20.467 --> 00:01:25.000
And your character, Dolores,
died at the end of last season.

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:26.801
-Spoiler alert.
[ Laughs ]

00:01:26.801 --> 00:01:28.734
-We can say that.
-Yeah, catch up, guys, come on.

00:01:28.734 --> 00:01:31.734
-Yeah, exactly, yeah.
But you're still on the show.

00:01:31.734 --> 00:01:34.133
Who are you playing on the show
this season?

00:01:34.133 --> 00:01:37.434
-This season, I am playing
a character called Christina,

00:01:37.434 --> 00:01:41.234
who is much more human, much
more vulnerable, very nerdy.

00:01:41.234 --> 00:01:44.334
She's a writer
and a video-game programmer.

00:01:44.334 --> 00:01:46.167
-Wow.
Okay.

00:01:46.167 --> 00:01:49.834
I love the show because, really,

00:01:49.834 --> 00:01:51.234
the writing
takes it to the next level.

00:01:51.234 --> 00:01:52.534
-Yes.
-And you don't really know

00:01:52.534 --> 00:01:54.400
what's gonna happen.
There's always a good twist.

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:56.434
And you don't know -- "Wait.
Is that person dead,

00:01:56.434 --> 00:01:58.634
or, no, they're back,
or are they a robot?"

00:01:58.634 --> 00:02:01.167
-You never really know
if you're dead on "Westworld."

00:02:01.167 --> 00:02:03.367
'Cause clearly,
they can just bring you

00:02:03.367 --> 00:02:05.234
right back as somebody else.
It doesn't matter, really.

00:02:05.234 --> 00:02:07.267
-Yeah, yeah.
And James Marsden is back.

00:02:07.267 --> 00:02:09.300
-James Marsden is back!
Yes.

00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:10.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:10.701 --> 00:02:13.367
-I mean, he was gone
for an entire season.

00:02:13.367 --> 00:02:15.133
-He was gone
for an entire season.

00:02:15.133 --> 00:02:16.701
They really wanted
to fake people out.

00:02:16.701 --> 00:02:18.968
And I was so dedicated
to keeping the secret

00:02:18.968 --> 00:02:21.000
that I lied to my own mother.

00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:22.434
[ Audience "Oohs" ]
-Really?

00:02:22.434 --> 00:02:24.834
-Whose dog is named Teddy,
by the way.

00:02:24.834 --> 00:02:26.901
So this was a big deal for her.

00:02:26.901 --> 00:02:29.334
And she was like,
"Wait, wait. Is it real?"

00:02:29.334 --> 00:02:30.534
And I was like, "Yeah, man.
I don't know.

00:02:30.534 --> 00:02:32.634
I mean, it's 'Westworld,'
so you never really know,

00:02:32.634 --> 00:02:34.367
but, like, I'm pretty sure
he's dead, dude."

00:02:34.367 --> 00:02:36.167
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, my gosh!

00:02:36.167 --> 00:02:38.267
-And so, yeah, yeah,
we had to stretch it out

00:02:38.267 --> 00:02:40.434
as long as possible.
-I love you do that.

00:02:40.434 --> 00:02:42.000
What can we say?
'Cause I don't want to give

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:43.901
any spoilers
besides what I just said

00:02:43.901 --> 00:02:45.467
that anyone died
could come back.

00:02:45.467 --> 00:02:49.968
But what can we say about
the new season of the show?

00:02:49.968 --> 00:02:51.400
-Nothing.
-Yeah.

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:52.901
[ Laughter ]
I mean, really you can't, right?

00:02:52.901 --> 00:02:55.801
This Sunday.
-This Sunday, it takes place

00:02:55.801 --> 00:02:58.501
in New York --
in a futuristic New York City.

00:02:58.501 --> 00:03:02.133
[ Cheers and applause ]
-That's where we do our show.

00:03:02.133 --> 00:03:04.701
-So...
-I could've been in this.

00:03:04.701 --> 00:03:06.067
-A cyborg version of you...
-Yes.

00:03:06.067 --> 00:03:08.200
-...should've been in season 4.
-Who do I gotta call? JJ?

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:11.067
-Just your head on the desk.
-Oh, my God, how creepy.

00:03:11.067 --> 00:03:13.701
Yeah, hologram head?
[ Laughter ]

00:03:13.701 --> 00:03:16.200
It's always good and well-done,
and we love it when you come on.

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:17.601
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:03:17.601 --> 00:03:19.367
Here's Evan Rachel Wood in the
new season of "Westworld."

00:03:19.367 --> 00:03:20.767
Take a look.

00:03:20.767 --> 00:03:29.100
♪♪

00:03:29.100 --> 00:03:32.801
-Record pitch.

00:03:32.801 --> 00:03:35.934
There's a young girl.

00:03:35.934 --> 00:03:37.834
Not that young.

00:03:37.834 --> 00:03:41.901
More like late teens.

00:03:41.901 --> 00:03:45.701
She lives at home with her
father in the country.

00:03:45.701 --> 00:03:48.300
[ Birds chirping ]

00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:53.000
Scratch that -- the city.

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:54.534
He's a little infirmed,
so she spends

00:03:54.534 --> 00:03:56.601
most of her time with him.

00:03:56.601 --> 00:03:59.200
But she dreams of a bigger life

00:03:59.200 --> 00:04:04.334
with excitement,
adventure, romance.

00:04:04.334 --> 00:04:05.901
-I mean, come on.
That is --

00:04:05.901 --> 00:04:07.968
-What does it all mean?

00:04:07.968 --> 00:04:10.601
-What does it all mean?
But that is --

00:04:10.601 --> 00:04:13.133
That is the future.

00:04:13.133 --> 00:04:14.567
-It is.
It really is.

00:04:14.567 --> 00:04:16.300
I mean, I think, in a few years,
people will realize

00:04:16.300 --> 00:04:17.901
that "Westworld"
was sort of a documentary.

00:04:17.901 --> 00:04:20.634
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah, exactly.

00:04:20.634 --> 00:04:21.834
I want to ask you about this.

00:04:21.834 --> 00:04:23.334
There's a photo
that's been going around.

00:04:23.334 --> 00:04:26.501
You're playing Madonna.
-I am playing Madonna.

00:04:26.501 --> 00:04:29.834
-In the Weird Al biopic.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:29.834 --> 00:04:31.934
-In the Weird Al biopic, yes.

00:04:31.934 --> 00:04:34.067
-What was your reaction
when you were asked to play her?

00:04:34.067 --> 00:04:35.968
-Honestly, like, I thought
I was gonna take a break

00:04:35.968 --> 00:04:37.667
for the rest of the year,
and then I got an e-mail,

00:04:37.667 --> 00:04:39.367
and the first thing I read is,

00:04:39.367 --> 00:04:41.501
"You've been offered the role
of Madonna,"

00:04:41.501 --> 00:04:44.133
and I just burst out laughing.
It was like --

00:04:44.133 --> 00:04:45.968
Like you just spit your drink
out when you read that.

00:04:45.968 --> 00:04:47.100
You know?
Like, it's just --

00:04:47.100 --> 00:04:49.300
You're not expecting that
on a Tuesday.

00:04:49.300 --> 00:04:52.367
And then I was like,
"Oh, God, do I want to do this?

00:04:52.367 --> 00:04:53.734
This is, like,
a lot of responsibility."

00:04:53.734 --> 00:04:55.868
But it's in a comedy.

00:04:55.868 --> 00:04:57.367
It's not a Madonna biopic.

00:04:57.367 --> 00:04:58.767
-You don't think
you would do a Madonna --

00:04:58.767 --> 00:05:00.467
-I think that would be
way too much pressure.

00:05:00.467 --> 00:05:02.234
Like, I don't know.
So like, as a comedy --

00:05:02.234 --> 00:05:04.567
-I mean, you nailed the look.
-Yeah.

00:05:04.567 --> 00:05:07.834
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:07.834 --> 00:05:10.400
-Do you -- Do you --
So, so you talk like Madonna?

00:05:10.400 --> 00:05:13.133
How does Madonna talk?
-It was a specific Madonna.

00:05:13.133 --> 00:05:15.133
You know,
it's early '80s Madonna.

00:05:15.133 --> 00:05:16.968
[ As Madonna ]
And early '80s Madonna,

00:05:16.968 --> 00:05:18.534
she really --
you know, she was very nasally,

00:05:18.534 --> 00:05:21.033
and everything she said
was very intentional.

00:05:21.033 --> 00:05:23.701
[ Laughter ]
And she disarms everyone

00:05:23.701 --> 00:05:26.400
that interviews her
by sort of looking at them.

00:05:26.400 --> 00:05:29.133
-Wow!
And have you talked to Madonna?

00:05:29.133 --> 00:05:30.501
Does Madonna know
you're playing her?

00:05:30.501 --> 00:05:32.567
-[ Normal voice ] No!
[ Laughter ]

00:05:32.567 --> 00:05:34.567
-Are you scared?
-I'm a little scared.

00:05:34.567 --> 00:05:36.634
I mean, it was like
halfway through filming,

00:05:36.634 --> 00:05:39.901
and I just assumed -- they've
obviously cleared this with her.

00:05:39.901 --> 00:05:42.501
And then halfway through
filming, I looked at them,

00:05:42.501 --> 00:05:44.934
I was like, "Yeah, so you guys
obviously talked to Madonna.

00:05:44.934 --> 00:05:46.634
How'd it go?"
And they were like...

00:05:46.634 --> 00:05:48.601
[ Laughter ]

00:05:48.601 --> 00:05:50.334
-"We..."
-I was like, "Oh, great.

00:05:50.334 --> 00:05:51.667
Now -- great, thanks, guys.

00:05:51.667 --> 00:05:53.834
You just put me on bad terms
with Madonna."

00:05:53.834 --> 00:05:55.200
[ Laughter ]
-No, no!

00:05:55.200 --> 00:05:56.868
Yeah, you don't want to be
on the bad side of Madonna.

00:05:56.868 --> 00:05:59.767
-No! I love Madonna.
-Me too.

00:05:59.767 --> 00:06:02.133
Do you get to sing
as Madonna, as well?

00:06:02.133 --> 00:06:04.467
-No. I sang --
We had, like, a karaoke

00:06:04.467 --> 00:06:08.501
wrap party, and I sang Madonna,
and then the director goes,

00:06:08.501 --> 00:06:10.834
"Why didn't I make you sing
in this movie?"

00:06:10.834 --> 00:06:13.534
-Yeah.
-I did. I can sing like Madonna.

00:06:13.534 --> 00:06:15.300
-Yeah, I mean you --
-I have to be able to sing

00:06:15.300 --> 00:06:17.734
like a lot of different people
'cause I have my band,

00:06:17.734 --> 00:06:20.167
Evan + Zane, and we do
so many different genres

00:06:20.167 --> 00:06:21.400
and so many different styles.

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:22.467
-We always have --

00:06:22.467 --> 00:06:24.100
We always have
a microphone here.

00:06:24.100 --> 00:06:26.334
-Oh, my God.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:26.334 --> 00:06:30.801
-We have the best band
in the world.

00:06:30.801 --> 00:06:32.133
Would you do it?
-Okay.

00:06:32.133 --> 00:06:33.367
I'll do it, I'll do it.
Okay.

00:06:33.367 --> 00:06:34.868
[ Laughing ]

00:06:34.868 --> 00:06:36.033
♪♪

00:06:36.033 --> 00:06:41.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:41.467 --> 00:06:44.467
♪ They can beg,
and they can plead ♪

00:06:44.467 --> 00:06:48.901
♪ But they can't see the light ♪

00:06:48.901 --> 00:06:52.067
♪ 'Cause the boy
with the cold hard cash ♪

00:06:52.067 --> 00:06:55.801
♪ Is always Mister Right ♪

00:06:55.801 --> 00:06:59.634
♪ 'Cause we are living
in a material world ♪

00:06:59.634 --> 00:07:02.601
♪ And I am a material girl ♪

00:07:02.601 --> 00:07:07.267
♪ You know that we are
living in a material world ♪

00:07:07.267 --> 00:07:10.300
♪ And I am a material girl ♪

00:07:10.300 --> 00:07:13.033
-Wait. What? How?!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:13.033 --> 00:07:15.634
How?!
How do you do everything?

00:07:15.634 --> 00:07:16.868
-I don't know.

00:07:16.868 --> 00:07:19.167
-How do you do everything?
-My job.

00:07:19.167 --> 00:07:21.167
-That was fantastic.

00:07:21.167 --> 00:07:23.133
Do you do
any other musical impressions?

00:07:23.133 --> 00:07:25.701
-Yeah.
Do you know any Alanis?

00:07:25.701 --> 00:07:27.167
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:27.167 --> 00:07:28.934
♪♪

00:07:28.934 --> 00:07:30.601
-1, 2, 3!

00:07:30.601 --> 00:07:32.734
♪ And I'm here ♪

00:07:32.734 --> 00:07:35.067
♪ To remind you ♪

00:07:35.067 --> 00:07:39.767
♪ Of the mess you left
when you went away ♪

00:07:39.767 --> 00:07:42.167
♪ It's not fair ♪

00:07:42.167 --> 00:07:44.400
♪ To deny me ♪

00:07:44.400 --> 00:07:48.834
♪ Of the cross I bear
that you gave to me ♪

00:07:48.834 --> 00:07:51.801
♪ You, you, you oughta know ♪

00:07:51.801 --> 00:07:54.667
-What in the what?!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:54.667 --> 00:07:58.167
-[ Laughs ]
-What in the world is going on?!

00:07:58.167 --> 00:08:01.067
What is going on?

00:08:01.067 --> 00:08:03.033
Do you have any more?
Is that all you got?

00:08:03.033 --> 00:08:04.968
-Let's do Janis!
Let's do Joplin!

00:08:04.968 --> 00:08:06.467
-You do Janis Joplin?
-Yes!

00:08:06.467 --> 00:08:08.300
-Roots, do you know, uh...

00:08:08.300 --> 00:08:11.667
♪♪

00:08:11.667 --> 00:08:17.434
-♪ Now come on, come on,
come on, come on ♪

00:08:17.434 --> 00:08:18.868
♪ Yeah, take it ♪

00:08:18.868 --> 00:08:22.701
♪ Take another little piece
of my heart now, baby ♪

00:08:22.701 --> 00:08:24.601
♪ Yeah ♪
-♪ Break it ♪

00:08:24.601 --> 00:08:29.033
♪ Break another little piece
of my heart, darlin', yeah ♪

00:08:29.033 --> 00:08:31.601
-♪ Come on ♪
-♪ Have another little piece

00:08:31.601 --> 00:08:34.934
♪ Of my heart now, baby ♪

00:08:34.934 --> 00:08:40.200
♪ You know you got it, child,
if it makes you feel good ♪

00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:43.000
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:43.000 --> 00:08:45.133
-Evan Rachel Wood, everybody!

00:08:45.133 --> 00:08:47.334
Come on!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:47.334 --> 00:08:49.334
"Westworld" returns
for it's fourth season

